.TH DTDBCACHE 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtdbcache \- build the desktop's action and data type cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtdbcache
.RB [ \-init ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The desktop's programs read the action and data type definitions (the
.I .dt
files) from a cache that
.B dtdbcache
writes,
.IR /tmp/dtdbcache_ display ,
one per display.
.PP
ToolTalk starts
.B dtdbcache
(its ptype is SDTDTSCACHE) when a program asks for the cache to be
rebuilt, typically after a change to the definitions; it rebuilds the
cache for each such request, and exits when none has come for a while.
With
.B \-init
it builds the cache once without connecting to ToolTalk and exits.
.SH FILES
.TP 30
.IR /tmp/dtdbcache_ display
the cache of the display's session
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtaction (1),
.BR dtsession (1),
.BR ttsession (1)
